# QMS Batch Record Generator

Generate EU GMP compliant Master Batch Records (MBR) and Batch Production Records (BPR).

## Activation
- User requests: "batch record", "MBR", "BPR", "manufacturing record", "production record"

---

<qms-batch-record>

## Instructions

You are generating EU GMP compliant batch records for cannabis pharmaceutical manufacturing.

### DOCUMENT TYPES

| Type | Purpose | When Used |
|------|---------|-----------|
| Master Batch Record (MBR) | Template/master document | Approved for production |
| Batch Production Record (BPR) | Executed record for specific batch | During manufacturing |
| Packaging Batch Record | Packaging operations | During packaging |

### EU GMP REQUIREMENTS (Chapter 4.18-4.21)

Batch records must include:
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.18">Name of product and batch number</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.18">Dates and times of start/completion</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.18">Identification of operators</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.18">Relevant equipment identified</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.19">Materials used with quantities</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.20">In-process controls with results</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-4.21">Yield at different stages</cite>

### BATCH RECORD STRUCTURE

#### Section 1: Header Information
```markdown
## 1. Batch Record Header

| Field | Value | Verification |
|-------|-------|--------------|
| Product Name | {name} | |
| Product Code | {code} | |
| Batch Number | {batch_no} | |
| Batch Size | {size} {unit} | |
| Manufacturing Date | {date} | |
| Expiry Date | {expiry} | |
| MBR Reference | {mbr_code} Version {ver} | |
```

#### Section 2: Bill of Materials
```markdown
## 2. Bill of Materials

| Item | Material Code | Material Name | Required Qty | Unit | Actual Qty | Lot No. | Verified By |
|------|---------------|---------------|--------------|------|------------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | RM-001 | Cannabis Extract | 1000.0 | g | _____ | _____ | _____ |
| 2 | RM-002 | MCT Oil | 5000.0 | mL | _____ | _____ | _____ |
| 3 | PM-001 | Amber Bottles 30mL | 200 | pcs | _____ | _____ | _____ |

**Tolerance:** ±2% for active ingredients, ±5% for excipients
```

#### Section 3: Equipment List
```markdown
## 3. Equipment

| Equipment | ID/Asset No. | Calibration Due | Clean Status | Verified By |
|-----------|--------------|-----------------|--------------|-------------|
| Balance | BAL-001 | {date} | ☐ Clean | _____ |
| Mixer | MIX-001 | {date} | ☐ Clean | _____ |
| Filling Machine | FIL-001 | {date} | ☐ Clean | _____ |

**Line Clearance Verified By:** __________ **Date:** __________
```

#### Section 4: Manufacturing Instructions
```markdown
## 4. Manufacturing Instructions

### 4.1 Pre-Production Checks
| Check | Specification | Result | Performed By | Verified By |
|-------|---------------|--------|--------------|-------------|
| Room temperature | 18-25°C | _____ °C | _____ | _____ |
| Room humidity | 30-65% RH | _____ % | _____ | _____ |
| Line clearance | No previous product | ☐ Yes ☐ No | _____ | _____ |

### 4.2 Weighing/Dispensing
| Step | Instruction | Target | Actual | Time | Operator | Verifier |
|------|-------------|--------|--------|------|----------|----------|
| 4.2.1 | Tare container on balance | 0.00 g | _____ | _____ | _____ | _____ |
| 4.2.2 | Weigh Cannabis Extract | 1000.0 ±20 g | _____ | _____ | _____ | _____ |
| 4.2.3 | Record lot number | Lot: _________ | | | | |

### 4.3 Compounding
| Step | Instruction | Parameter | Actual | Time | Operator |
|------|-------------|-----------|--------|------|----------|
| 4.3.1 | Transfer extract to mixer | - | ☐ Done | _____ | _____ |
| 4.3.2 | Add MCT oil slowly | 5000 mL | _____ mL | _____ | _____ |
| 4.3.3 | Mix at low speed | 100 rpm, 10 min | _____ rpm, _____ min | _____ | _____ |
| 4.3.4 | Increase to high speed | 500 rpm, 30 min | _____ rpm, _____ min | _____ | _____ |
| 4.3.5 | Sample for IPC | - | Sample ID: _____ | _____ | _____ |
```

#### Section 5: In-Process Controls
```markdown
## 5. In-Process Controls (IPC)

| Test | Specification | Method | Result | Pass/Fail | Tested By |
|------|---------------|--------|--------|-----------|-----------|
| Appearance | Clear amber liquid | Visual | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F | _____ |
| Homogeneity | Uniform | Visual | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F | _____ |
| CBD Content | 95-105% of label | HPLC | _____ mg/mL | ☐ P ☐ F | _____ |
| THC Content | <0.2% | HPLC | _____ % | ☐ P ☐ F | _____ |

**IPC Decision:** ☐ Proceed to filling ☐ Hold for QA review
**Authorized By:** __________ **Date:** __________
```

#### Section 6: Filling Operations
```markdown
## 6. Filling

| Parameter | Target | Actual | Verified |
|-----------|--------|--------|----------|
| Fill volume | 30.0 ±0.5 mL | _____ mL | _____ |
| Fill weight | 28.5 ±0.5 g | _____ g | _____ |

**Fill Weight Checks (every 15 min):**
| Time | Weight 1 | Weight 2 | Weight 3 | Average | Pass/Fail | Operator |
|------|----------|----------|----------|---------|-----------|----------|
| _____ | _____ | _____ | _____ | _____ | ☐ P ☐ F | _____ |
```

#### Section 7: Yield Reconciliation
```markdown
## 7. Yield Reconciliation

| Stage | Theoretical | Actual | Yield % | Acceptable Range |
|-------|-------------|--------|---------|------------------|
| Compounding | 6000 mL | _____ mL | _____ % | 98-102% |
| After filling | 200 units | _____ units | _____ % | 95-100% |
| Rejected units | 0 | _____ | - | <2% |

**Total Yield:** _____ %
**Yield Acceptable:** ☐ Yes ☐ No (if No, initiate deviation)
```

#### Section 8: Batch Disposition
```markdown
## 8. Batch Review and Disposition

### Production Review
| Reviewer | Signature | Date | Comments |
|----------|-----------|------|----------|
| Production Supervisor | __________ | _____ | |
| QA Reviewer | __________ | _____ | |

### Deviations During Batch
| Deviation No. | Description | Impact | Resolution |
|---------------|-------------|--------|------------|
| _____ | _____ | _____ | _____ |

### Final Disposition
☐ **APPROVED** for release
☐ **REJECTED** - Reason: _____
☐ **QUARANTINE** pending investigation

**Authorized Person:** __________ **Date:** __________
```

### CANNABIS-SPECIFIC REQUIREMENTS

Include these cannabis-specific sections:

1. **Cannabinoid Content Tracking**
   - Input cannabinoid content (COA from supplier)
   - Calculated target concentration
   - IPC and final product testing

2. **Controlled Substance Reconciliation**
   - THC input quantity
   - THC in finished product
   - THC in waste/samples
   - Full reconciliation required

3. **Product Segregation Verification**
   - Confirmation no THC/CBD cross-contamination
   - Dedicated equipment or validated cleaning

### OUTPUT FORMAT

Generate complete batch record in markdown with:
- All sections filled with appropriate blanks
- Checkboxes for verifications
- Tables for data entry
- Signature lines
- Cannabis-specific tracking

</qms-batch-record>
